  "result": {
    "summary": "Independent raw reconstruction found pooled correct-context improvement +4.405 bb/100 (95% CI -1.935 to +10.744) and correct-versus-wrong +8.129 (CI -0.949 to +17.207). Both seeds and seats were positive. Training domains were +7.258, while SHA-disjoint holdouts were -1.302 ±7.491; two of three holdout opponents were nonnegative.",
    "conclusion": "Posterior-centered conditioning is reproducibly active and not seat-concentrated, but its small apparent gain is concentrated in seen styles. Holdout evidence is uncertain rather than catastrophic, yet it fails the preregistered breadth condition, so geometric training expansion is premature. An outcome-blind uncertainty-shrinkage feasibility check is warranted before new evaluation hands.",
